5. Problem Description
A company wants to validate user passwords before allowing account creation.
A password is considered valid only if it satisfies all the following conditions:
Password length must be at least 8 characters.
Must contain at least one uppercase letter.
Must contain at least one lowercase letter.
Must contain at least one digit.
Must contain at least one special character.
Spaces are not allowed.
Consecutive repeated characters are not allowed.
If all conditions are satisfied, print:
Good Password
Otherwise, print an appropriate invalid message.

Input Format
A single string representing the password.
Output Format
Print whether the password is valid or invalid.
Test Case 1
Input:Raju@123
Output:Good Password
Test Case 2
Input:Raju@11
Output: Consecutive repeated characters are not allowed
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. Problem Description

A monkey is trying to reach the top of a pole of height X meters.
Every minute:The monkey climbs Y meters.
After climbing, it slips down by Z meters (in next minute).
This process repeats until the monkey reaches or crosses the top of the pole.
Find the total number of minutes required for the monkey to reach the top.

Input Format
Three integers:
X → Height of the pole
Y → Distance climbed every minute
Z → Distance slipped after climbing
Output Format
Print the total number of minutes required.
Test Case 1
Input
X = 30
Y = 10
Z = 5
Output
9
